143
00:11:00,979 --> 00:11:03,459
Could Straw Hat be Roger's successor?

144
00:11:03,459 --> 00:11:06,899
Straw Hat may be Ace's brother, but he's not Gold Rogers' son.

145
00:11:06,899 --> 00:11:08,659
This whole thing is weird.

146
00:11:08,659 --> 00:11:12,739
Wow, no matter how you spin it, this story is going to be huge!

147
00:11:12,739 --> 00:11:21,939
This article's already been circulated throughout the entire world.

148
00:11:21,939 --> 00:11:26,899
Those journalists are so starved for attention, they even mentioned how Straw Hat escaped.

149
00:11:26,899 --> 00:11:30,819
This is humiliating!

150
00:11:30,819 --> 00:11:46,659
If we take this appearance of his at face value, all Straw Hat did was pay tribute to his brother,

151
00:11:46,659 --> 00:11:49,379
Ace, Whitebeard, and all the other people who died in the war.

152
00:11:49,379 --> 00:11:54,019
The moment of silence and trip around Marine Ford support that notion.

153
00:11:54,019 --> 00:11:56,499
But he rung the bell not twice as is customary.

154
00:11:56,499 --> 00:12:00,899
But a whopping 16 times! 16 bell tolls!

155
00:12:00,899 --> 00:12:03,539
There's no doubt in my mind that this is a challenge to us!

156
00:12:03,539 --> 00:12:09,699
Oh, honestly, for such a rookie, this Straw Hat Luffy is certainly controversial.

157
00:12:09,699 --> 00:12:14,019
But the boy is Garp's grandson, so I suppose I shouldn't be surprised.

158
00:12:14,019 --> 00:12:16,979
I'm curious as to how he and Rayleigh know each other.

159
00:12:17,539 --> 00:12:20,659
I highly doubt Rayleigh intended to rejoin the fray.

160
00:12:21,379 --> 00:12:24,019
A pity Jinbei decided to turn against us.

161
00:12:24,019 --> 00:12:29,379
His allegiance to the world government as a warlord acted as a symbol of inter-tribal peace.

162
00:12:29,379 --> 00:12:31,299
It's disappointing to lose him.

163
00:12:31,299 --> 00:12:35,219
Thanks to this turmoil, the three great powers are completely unbalanced.

164
00:12:35,219 --> 00:12:38,739
Also, how should we take care of the vacancies among the seven warlords?

165
00:12:38,739 --> 00:12:42,339
First, we need to observe what will unfold in the new world.

166
00:12:42,339 --> 00:12:45,859
Relationships and hierarchies among pirates are sure to change.

167
00:12:45,859 --> 00:12:49,299
We must take great care in ensuring we pick the most powerful ones.

168
00:12:49,299 --> 00:12:53,779
Blackbeard already made his first move in the new world, by the way.

169
00:12:53,779 --> 00:12:58,739
He knocked off a promising rookie, one that had a bounty of over 100 million berries.

170
00:12:58,739 --> 00:13:03,939
And thanks to his time with Whitebeard, he knows all about the old man's territory.

171
00:13:03,939 --> 00:13:09,699
He certainly has a lead over any other pirate who's aiming to become one of the four emperors.

172
00:13:11,459 --> 00:13:16,899
No one else in history has ever eaten two devil fruits, yet he seems to have absorbed Whitebeards.

173
00:13:17,459 --> 00:13:20,499
The only ones with the power to stop him are the other emperors.

174
00:13:21,459 --> 00:13:27,619
Actually, perhaps Marco the Phoenix and the other Whitebeard survivors have a small chance as well.

175
00:13:27,619 --> 00:13:33,619
It's always the D's who stir up the most trouble. First Roger, then Portgus.

176
00:13:34,179 --> 00:13:47,619
And now, with Monkey D. Luffy, those names are exposed to the public far more than they should be.

177
00:13:47,619 --> 00:14:01,939
I tried to talk him out of it, but as far as we're concerned, Garp is practically retired.

178
00:14:03,299 --> 00:14:07,139
Though he does technically hold his title, so he's still a navy officer.

179
00:14:07,939 --> 00:14:10,979
We need him to stay on board to train our young soldiers.

180
00:14:10,979 --> 00:14:18,499
If you intend to resign from your position as Fleet Admiral, could you at least do that for us as well, Sengoku?

181
00:14:19,619 --> 00:14:26,659
Yes, sir. I can accept that offer. It's not the worst way to spend retired life.

182
00:14:26,659 --> 00:14:34,419
The two central figures who have led the navy since Roger's era are finally stepping down.

183
00:14:34,419 --> 00:14:39,299
This will make quite a splash, I fear. Needless to say, you'll be missed.

184
00:14:39,299 --> 00:14:44,099
Including the prisoners that were set free from the sixth level of Impel Down.

185
00:14:44,099 --> 00:14:46,659
There's still a mess of dangerous pirates on the loose.

186
00:14:49,459 --> 00:14:52,899
Before his death, Newgate was at the top of the list.

187
00:14:52,899 --> 00:14:58,019
The great pirate era is in a period of transition.

188
00:14:58,739 --> 00:15:01,539
Old navy officers shouldn't keep clinging to power.

189
00:15:02,419 --> 00:15:06,019
The basis for justice changes from era to era.

190
00:15:08,499 --> 00:15:10,579
It sounds like you're ready to step down.

191
00:15:10,579 --> 00:15:14,179
Oh, Kong, while I'm here, I would like to recommend

192
00:15:14,179 --> 00:15:17,219
Aokiji to take my place as the next Fleet Admiral.

193
00:15:17,219 --> 00:15:18,499
He'd do a fine job.

194
00:15:22,899 --> 00:15:27,379
They call this power Haki.

195
00:15:28,899 --> 00:15:30,739
I'm certain that's what you've got.

196
00:15:32,339 --> 00:15:35,619
Perhaps it was weakened by the trauma you experienced during the war.

197
00:15:36,419 --> 00:15:40,819
Normally, the only way you could obtain the power of Haki is through vigorous training.

198
00:15:40,819 --> 00:15:43,619
Haki? Are you sure, Doc?

199
00:15:43,619 --> 00:15:48,739
You're pretty lucky, kid. It's the same power that the navy vice-admirals have in their possession.

200
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:54,099
Really?

201
00:16:02,339 --> 00:16:05,059
I can feel all those people echoing in my head.

202
00:16:05,619 --> 00:16:06,819
I can't make it stop.

203
00:16:07,379 --> 00:16:10,419
You two are apprentices to Vice Admiral Garp, right?

204
00:16:10,419 --> 00:16:11,459
Ask him about it.

205
00:16:11,459 --> 00:16:15,299
Hey, Doctor! You think I might pick up some Haki too?

206
00:16:15,299 --> 00:16:16,819
I doubt it.

207
00:16:19,219 --> 00:16:20,259
It's not fair!

208
00:16:20,259 --> 00:16:23,699
Damn it! We were partners and all of a sudden you're way cooler than me!

209
00:16:24,499 --> 00:16:26,339
I don't know how to feel about all this.

210
00:16:27,379 --> 00:16:28,819
But I do know how I feel.

211
00:16:29,459 --> 00:16:29,859
Weird.

212
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:32,819
It's like I'm a completely different person.

213
00:16:33,379 --> 00:16:36,019
But if this thing that happened to me really is Haki,

214
00:16:36,499 --> 00:16:38,739
I might be able to use it to get stronger.

215
00:16:39,699 --> 00:16:41,379
Much stronger than I am right now.

216
00:16:41,379 --> 00:16:44,899
Maybe even as strong as him. For real this time.

217
00:16:47,299 --> 00:16:50,659
I'm sorry, Admiral Kichi! We couldn't hold the fort!

218
00:16:55,699 --> 00:16:56,419
It's fine.

219
00:16:56,419 --> 00:16:57,139
Huh?

220
00:17:02,739 --> 00:17:04,019
Alive after all.

221
00:17:05,059 --> 00:17:06,179
Would you look at that?

222
00:17:07,059 --> 00:17:09,939
You hear about Straw Hat going back to Marineford?

223
00:17:09,939 --> 00:17:11,139
Crazy, kid.

224
00:17:11,139 --> 00:17:11,939
Yeah.

225
00:17:11,939 --> 00:17:14,819
The War of the Best is still fresh in everyone's minds,

226
00:17:14,819 --> 00:17:17,859
and now Straw Hat rings the bell 16 times.

227
00:17:17,859 --> 00:17:19,939
Is he trying to send some kind of message or what?

228
00:17:21,699 --> 00:17:22,339
Beats me.

229
00:17:23,699 --> 00:17:26,659
Anyway, did you ask them about my transfer?

230
00:17:26,659 --> 00:17:30,819
Not yet, but I'll be sure to bring it up with Sengoku when I have the chance.

231
00:17:30,819 --> 00:17:32,499
Are you serious about this?

232
00:17:32,499 --> 00:17:35,699
Not really the sort of thing somebody would make a joke about, is it?

233
00:17:35,699 --> 00:17:37,619
No, especially not you.

234
00:17:37,619 --> 00:17:41,379
But either way, people aren't exactly clamoring to join G5.

235
00:17:41,939 --> 00:17:43,779
I'm sure you've heard the stories.

236
00:17:44,259 --> 00:17:45,139
It's not pretty.

237
00:17:46,339 --> 00:17:49,459
So transferring to the fifth branch on the Grand Line, huh?

238
00:17:50,419 --> 00:17:51,459
The new world.

239
00:17:51,459 --> 00:17:54,019
You realize how wild things get over there.

240
00:17:54,019 --> 00:17:57,539
For me, it's better to be closer to my target.

241
00:17:57,539 --> 00:18:04,179
The news about Straw Hat Luffy quickly spread through countless waters.

242
00:18:05,779 --> 00:18:08,259
Word even spread to the new world.

243
00:18:08,259 --> 00:18:12,259
Straw Hat Luffy. Turns out the punk is still alive.

244
00:18:12,979 --> 00:18:16,899
He rang the bell 16 times to mark a new era in Marineford.

245
00:18:16,899 --> 00:18:18,979
So, what the hell is this Ox Bell thing?

246
00:18:18,979 --> 00:18:25,299
A relic, you might say. It's a sacred bell from the Ox Lloyd.

247
00:18:25,859 --> 00:18:29,459
A Navy warship that was quite impressive back in its day.

248
00:18:30,339 --> 00:18:34,499
At year's end, they ring the bell eight times to signify the passing year.

249
00:18:35,059 --> 00:18:39,219
Then eight more times as a sort of good omen for the coming year.

250
00:18:39,219 --> 00:18:44,899
So that's the meaning of 16 rings. Some crusty old navy custom. Nothing special.

251
00:18:47,459 --> 00:18:54,259
But since the year hasn't ended yet, maybe Straw Hat did it to announce the end and beginning of a new pirate era.

252
00:18:54,259 --> 00:18:56,819
He came out of Marineford pretty cocky.

253
00:18:56,819 --> 00:19:00,259
Whitebeard's era's over and he's acting like he's in charge of the next one.

254
00:19:01,059 --> 00:19:05,139
Let the brat do what he wants. Everyone knows his brother's death hit him hard,

255
00:19:05,139 --> 00:19:08,419
so he's gotta make a good showing before people think he's washed up.

256
00:19:10,739 --> 00:19:13,059
He's gonna be a real pain in the ass.

257
00:19:13,059 --> 00:19:17,539
His bounty's through the roof and it's only going up if he keeps pulling stunts like this.

258
00:19:17,539 --> 00:19:19,299
Well, that's his plan, I'm sure.

259
00:19:20,419 --> 00:19:25,299
Too bad. I'm gonna teach him the hard way that he can't do whatever he wants. Not here.

260
00:19:28,259 --> 00:19:29,299
The new world.

261
00:19:30,179 --> 00:19:32,899
From how they talked this place up, I thought it'd be more fun.

262
00:19:33,539 --> 00:19:35,299
Not full of cowards like you.

263
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:40,259
What's the big idea, huh? Untie us right now. We didn't cause you any harm, did we?

264
00:19:40,259 --> 00:19:45,459
This place is a living hell. We were trying to sail away. Please let us go back to paradise alive!

265
00:19:46,019 --> 00:19:49,699
Paradise, huh? Do you mean your boring home that's pirate-free?

266
00:19:49,699 --> 00:19:55,139
You just got here so you don't know how horrible the sea really is! Free us and leave while you can!

267
00:20:02,899 --> 00:20:04,099
Straw head, huh?

268
00:20:04,099 --> 00:20:06,979
Yes, father. He's cooking something up again.

269
00:20:06,979 --> 00:20:12,019
No need to bother over that fool. If he keeps playing his cards so early, he'll burn out before

270
00:20:12,019 --> 00:20:14,739
the end of the game. What is it?

271
00:20:15,379 --> 00:20:20,499
Boss, come quick! It's the ship! It's not in the water! It's in the air!

272
00:20:20,499 --> 00:20:26,819
What do you mean? What's going on? How's this possible? Control the ship, damage!

273
00:20:26,819 --> 00:20:29,459
Look, bottom! Something is coming down from the sky!

274
00:20:29,459 --> 00:20:30,179
Gah!

275
00:20:32,499 --> 00:20:35,139
It's not coming down! We're going up!

276
00:20:35,139 --> 00:20:43,699
Wait. Who are you?

277
00:20:45,619 --> 00:20:49,939
I'm sorry. Could you say that again? I wasn't really listening to you.

278
00:20:50,819 --> 00:20:57,059
I'm Brownbeard. There's a bounty of over 80 million berries on my head. Are you listening now?

279
00:20:57,859 --> 00:21:04,339
This is my territory, so when you hear my name, you bow! You think you can sit your ass on my men and get

280
00:21:04,339 --> 00:21:07,299
away with it? You gotta pay for that with your own blood.

281
00:21:07,299 --> 00:21:14,099
I see. I thought I had misheard you because it's such a stupid name. I'll tell you two things.

282
00:21:14,739 --> 00:21:17,539
Number one is I do not appreciate your jokes.

283
00:21:17,539 --> 00:21:18,419
Is that so?

284
00:21:18,419 --> 00:21:25,699
As for number two, I can see the shadow of death crawling upon your face.

285
00:21:34,339 --> 00:21:38,739
And you're absolutely certain that's the island the log pose is pointing to?

286
00:21:39,379 --> 00:21:42,339
Just look at it. It's raining lightning.

287
00:21:43,139 --> 00:21:44,499
This isn't going to work.

288
00:21:44,499 --> 00:21:52,739
How the hell do we get to the shore?

289
00:21:55,299 --> 00:21:59,619
There is a realization that comes to all men who set foot in the new world.

290
00:21:59,619 --> 00:22:01,939
Hey, priest! Somebody is approaching!

291
00:22:02,659 --> 00:22:04,819
Huh? Who goes there?

292
00:22:04,819 --> 00:22:09,379
All their struggles in the first half of the Grand Line suddenly seem petty.

293
00:22:09,379 --> 00:22:12,179
Is that a young man waiting to greet me?

294
00:22:12,179 --> 00:22:14,659
What do you want from us, old lady?

295
00:22:14,659 --> 00:22:19,219
Because compared to this, those waters were like paradise.

296
00:22:21,459 --> 00:22:23,699
Would you like an umbrella for your journey?

297
00:22:23,699 --> 00:22:29,059
I'm telling you, if we stay here, we'll be dead! Every last one of us!

298
00:22:29,059 --> 00:22:33,379
Let us sail back to paradise! I promise we won't get in your way! I beg you!

299
00:22:33,379 --> 00:22:35,779
Man, this guy's a real wet blanket.

300
00:22:35,779 --> 00:22:43,059
Didn't you choose the life of a pirate? You're not prepared to die for that.

301
00:22:43,059 --> 00:22:46,259
Maybe you should have stayed away from the new world!

302
00:22:52,739 --> 00:22:55,859
You want to throw down the gauntlet straw hat? That's fine.

303
00:22:55,859 --> 00:22:59,219
But don't cry when I come for you, because it won't be pretty!

304
00:23:05,779 --> 00:23:14,499
Luffy's latest incident in Marineford quickly becomes worldwide news.

305
00:23:14,499 --> 00:23:19,859
Although his exploit was a success, it seems to cause little but bewilderment to all who hear it.

306
00:23:19,859 --> 00:23:24,979
His strange message has met its target, but will his friends understand the next stage of his plan?

307
00:23:24,979 --> 00:23:28,979
On the next One Piece! With hopes it will reach my friends!

308
00:23:28,979 --> 00:23:34,259
Big news spreading fast! I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

309
00:23:35,779 --> 00:23:41,059
But there is no persön 뭘 out of all locations here!

310
00:23:43,539 --> 00:23:47,059
There's also an outlet in the Washington Post here that without any thought,

311
00:23:47,059 --> 00:23:49,219
but that means I could double check!

312
00:23:49,219 --> 00:23:51,459
At the second one, monkey or liberaterina!

313
00:23:53,379 --> 00:23:55,059
Jacketでしょう?

314
00:23:55,059 --> 00:23:58,099
There is an outlet in the lifetake of all these reactions,

315
00:23:58,099 --> 00:23:59,219
so it's ayudar to fix.

316
00:23:59,219 --> 00:24:00,819
It's time to fix it!

